# Cloudflare Pages routing for the static brochure.
#
# The privacy policy is a REAL static file, not a router route:
# `npm run build:privacy` (scripts/build-promo-privacy.ts) writes
# public/privacy.html — plain HTML with no JavaScript — and Cloudflare Pages
# serves a static `foo.html` at the clean URL `/foo` with a direct 200.
#
# There is deliberately NO `/privacy` rule here. Verified locally with
# `wrangler pages dev`: adding `/privacy /privacy.html 200` produced
# `308 -> /privacy`, because Pages also canonicalises `/privacy.html` down to
# `/privacy`, and the rewrite re-triggers the same rule — an infinite loop on
# the one URL Google's reviewer and crawler must reach. Pages flagged it and
# ignored the rule; a real deployment would have failed the policy link.
#
# What the SPA fallback below does is serve every BrowserRouter path
# (/technology, /solutions, /download) from index.html. Static files take
# precedence over it, which is why /privacy answers with the policy on
# `pages dev`; the live deployment is re-probed after every change to this
# pairing, because the local emulator skips the wildcard rule entirely.
/*    /index.html    200
